 Nous voulons vous connaître
 *******************
 1-year temporary position with benefits (maternity leave replacement) - Jan. 2027  
 * possibility of extension or permanency at the end of the mandate  
 About Mila
 Founded by Professor Yoshua Bengio of the Université de Montréal, Mila brings together researchers specializing in artificial intelligence, and more specifically in machine learning, deep learning and reinforcement learning. Recognized worldwide for its important contributions to the field of deep learning, Mila has particularly distinguished itself in language modeling, machine translation, object recognition and generative models. Since 2017, Mila has been the fruit of a collaboration between Université de Montréal and McGill University, in close collaboration with Polytechnique Montréal and HEC Montréal. 
 Mila's mission is to be a global hub of scientific advances that inspires innovation and the rise of artificial intelligence (AI) for the benefit of all.
 Role description
 Are you looking for a stimulating and constantly evolving work environment? Are you interested in being at the forefront of the latest innovations and applications in artificial intelligence that can benefit society, and demonstrating their impact to the organization's stakeholders? Here is a golden opportunity to join a team driven by an engaging mission rooted in human values.
 Reporting to the Director, Data and Business Intelligence, the Impact and reporting Analyst is responsible for managing and carrying out accountability activities for funding bodies and other stakeholders, as well as managing processes and monitoring tools related to data management and performance indicators. Working closely with Mila's operational teams, the analyst plays a key role in showcasing and measuring the organization's impact at all levels, both to inform external stakeholders and to enable sound management of the organization by Mila's leadership. For example, they will contribute to deliverables such as Mila's Impact Reports .
 Finally, the Impact and reporting Analyst will have numerous opportunities to deepen their knowledge in business intelligence.
 Responsibilities
 Act as the lead in producing accountability reports for various funding bodies, in accordance with each organization's stakes, the strategic plan, and best practices;
 Collect, organize, and analyze data from multiple internal and external sources;
 Advise and innovate through the continuous improvement of processes, tools, or methodologies that can enhance organizational performance related to report development, particularly through artificial intelligence;
 Participate in the implementation of information collection and analysis tools;
 Work closely with the Business Intelligence Advisor to synchronize indicators with management dashboards;
 Draft the textual content of reports in collaboration with the leads across various internal teams;
 Maintain appropriate management and documentation tools to support these responsibilities (document management, task management, timelines, etc.);
 Help facilitate communication with funding bodies, particularly regarding timelines and reporting expectations;
 Inform and provide regular progress updates to Mila's leadership.
 Your profil
 Undergraduate university degree in administration or a relevant discipline;
 Minimum of 3 to 5 years of experience in data analysis (or related experience);
 Bilingual in French and English, due to interactions you will have with some of our partners, stakeholders, or members of our English-speaking academic community;
 Advanced knowledge of Google Workspace (Google Sheets) and/or Microsoft Office (Excel);
 Knowledge of Power BI, an asset;
 Excellent analytical and synthesis skills;
 Excellent organizational and planning skills, methodical and structured;
 Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously with tight deadlines;
 Strong interest in continuous improvement;
 Sense of initiative and intellectual curiosity;
 Experience in managing funding programs, an asset;
 Knowledge of academic and research culture, an asset.
 Great reasons to work at Mila
 An employee and family assistance program;
 Access to a telemedicine service;
 A collaborative and inclusive work environment.
